=== Coincidence check: does 1/8 in the digamma moment equal M1 structurally? ===
  full-line moment       = -0.36587750650535586986
  (1/2pi)int_R P * psi(1/2) = -0.49087750650535586986  [= (1/4)psi(1/2)]
  deviation piece        = 0.125   vs 1/8 = 0.125
  M1 (half-line)         = 0.125
  => the two '1/8's use DIFFERENT integration conventions (full vs half line).
Step 1: Fourier inversion (1/2pi)int_R P cos(lam t/2) dlam = 1/(4 cosh^2(t/4))
  t=0.7: rel=2.03316850359314533983082483784e-31
  t=3.0: rel=1.65286555234525748880528798601e-31
Step 2: moment = int_0^inf dt [1/(2 sinh(t/2))] * (1/4)[1 - sech^2(t/4)]
  = 0.125
Step 3: substitution u=t/4 gives (1/4) int_0^inf tanh u sech^2 u du = (1/4)(1/2) = 1/8
  = 0.125   [exact 1/8 = 0.125]
Cross-check vs direct digamma moment:
  0.125
